card.statement:
If $s\in\mf g_{\frac12}$ is embeddable, then $2s^*,4x,s$ is an $\mf{sl}_2$-triple and:

[(a)]

- $\mf g_0^s\subset\mf g_0^f$;

- the maps $\ad(f):\,\mf g^s_{\frac12}\to[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]\subset\mf g_{-\frac12}$, $\ad(s)\circ\ad(f):\,\mf g^s_{\frac12}\to[s,[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]]\subset\mf g_{0}$, and $\ad(s)\circ\ad(s)\circ\ad(f):\,\mf g^s_{\frac12}\to[s,[s,[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]]]\subset\mf g_{\frac12}$, are bijective;

- we have the orthogonal (w.r.t. $(\cdot\,|\,\cdot)$) decomposition $\mf g_0=\mf g_0^s\oplus[s,\mf g_{-\frac12}]$;

- we have the dual (w.r.t. $(\cdot\,|\,\cdot)$) decompositions $\mf g_{\frac12}=\mf g_{\frac12}^s\oplus\mb F[s^*,e]$, and $\mf g_{-\frac12}=\mf g_{-\frac12}^{s^*}\oplus\mb F[s,f]$;

- we have the orthogonal decompositions $\mf g_0=\mf g_0^f\oplus\mb Fx$, and $\mf g_0^f=\mf g_0^s\oplus[s,[f,\mf g^s_{\frac12}]]$;

- we have the dual (w.r.t. $(\cdot\,|\,\cdot)$) decompositions $\mf g_{\frac12}=[s,[s,[f,\mf g_{\frac12}^s]]]\oplus\mb Fs$, and $\mf g_{-\frac12}=[f,\mf g_{\frac12}^s]\oplus\mb Fs^*$;

- we have the dual (w.r.t. $(\cdot\,|\,\cdot)$) decompositions $\mf g_{\frac12}=[s,\mf g_0^f]\oplus\mb Fs$, and $\mf g_{-\frac12}=[s^*,\mf g_0^f]\oplus\mb Fs^*$;

- we have a non-degenerate, symmetric, $\mf g_0^s$-invariant bilinear form $\chi$ on $\mf g^s_{\frac12}$ given by $\chi(u,v)=([s,[f,u]]|[s,[f,v]])$.
